Regenerating people–nature relationships to counter biocultural erosion in the Amazon

Rebuilding the reciprocal care-oriented relationships between Amazonian Indigenous peoples and nature could address the predicted effects of climate change on biodiversity.





                By

Victoria Reyes-García ORCID: http://orcid.org/0000-0002-2914-80550

Victoria Reyes-García




                            Victoria Reyes-García is at the Catalan Institution for Research and Advanced Studies (ICREA), 08010 Barcelona, Spain, and the Institute of Environmental Sciences and Technology, and is in the Department of Social and Cultural Anthropology, Autonomous University of Barcelona (UAB).






